==Battleground==
*4 [[Duche]]s spawn, delay 1.67~5 seconds<sup>50f~150f</sup>.
*6 [[R.Ost]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 1~3 seconds<sup>30f~90f</sup>.
*2 [[Duche]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.

==Strategy==
It is recommended to use at least 4 meatshields. You can also use [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Dragon Cat]], [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Legs Cat]], and 3-4 main attackers. [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cats]] such as [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]], [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|Holy Valkyrie Cat]], [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Dark Emperor Catdam]], [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Red Riding Mina]], and/or [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cats]] if you have them.

Stall the [[Duche]]s and save money for the attackers. Also, you might need to spam your cats quickly, so you can use Cat CPU too. It might take a few tries to do it right.

==='''Strategy 1 ([[Cheese]])'''===
''This strategy is mainly for 2 to 4 crowns, as the Cats are hard to get before the first completion.''

{{Lineup
|Ururun Cat
|Executioner
|Evil Cat
|Mohawk Cat
|Crazed Dragon Cat
|Eraser Cat
|Manic Eraser Cat
|Macho Crystal Cat
|Lone Cat and Kitten
|Cat God the Great
|cannon = Breakerblast
|notes = [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Crystal Cat]] can be replaced by [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Cleanerbot Cat]] for more defense.
}}

'''Battle:''' Start by stalling the first four Duches with dual Erasers, and save up for Cat God the Great. Once you have enough money for him, spawn him in and save up for Tourist Cat. When Cat God is about to end his attack (where he does the most damage), fire your Breakerblast Cannon so that the Duches don't get hit. Timing here doesn't need to be exact, but try your best to make sure Cat God doesn't hit the Duches. Continue this cycle until you destroy the base.

